There are two classes of commands,  configuration  commands  that
configure  a  persistent association with a remote server or peer
or reference clock, and auxiliary commands that specify  environ‐
mental  variables  that  control various related operations.  The
various modes are determined by the command keyword and the  type
of the required IP address.  Addresses are classed by type as (s)
a  remote  server or peer (IPv4 class A, B and C), (b) the broad‐
cast address of a local interface, (m) a multicast address  (IPv4
class  D),  or (r) a reference clock address (127.127.x.x).  Note
that only those options applicable to each command are listed be‐
